       "content": "# Solving $(26^2 - 24^2 - 10)^2 - 10^2$\n\n## Step 1: Simplify $26^2 - 24^2$ using difference of squares\n\n$$26^2 - 24^2 = (26-24)(26+24) = 2 \\times 50 = 100$$\n\n## Step 2: Substitute back into the expression\n\n$$(100 - 10)^2 - 10^2 = 90^2 - 10^2$$\n\n## Step 3: Apply difference of squares again\n\n$$90^2 - 10^2 = (90-10)(90+10) = 80 \\times 100 = 8000$$\n\n$$\\boxed{8000}$$",
       "name": null,
       "reasoning": "We need to compute (26\u00b2 - 24\u00b2 - 10)\u00b2 - 10\u00b2.\n\nLet me work through this step by step.\n\nFirst, compute 26\u00b2 - 24\u00b2. I can use the difference of squares: 26\u00b2 - 24\u00b2 = (26-24)(26+24) = 2 \u00d7 50 = 100.\n\nSo the expression becomes (100 - 10)\u00b2 - 10\u00b2 = 90\u00b2 - 10\u00b2.\n\nNow 90\u00b2 - 10\u00b2 = (90-10)(90+10) = 80 \u00d7 100 = 8000.\n\nSo the answer is 8000.",
